          "tone": "neutral",
          "type": "code-block",
          "label": "queue.rs · Local::push_lifo / pop_lifo",
          "language": "rust",
          "code": "/// Pushes a task to the LIFO slot, returning the task previously in the\n/// LIFO slot (if there was one).\npub(crate) fn push_lifo(&self, task: task::Notified<T>) -> Option<task::Notified<T>> {\n    self.inner.lifo.swap(Some(task))\n}\n\n/// Pops the task currently held in the LIFO slot, if there is one;\n/// otherwise, returns `None`.\npub(crate) fn pop_lifo(&self) -> Option<task::Notified<T>> {\n    // LIFO-suction!\n    self.inner.lifo.take()\n}",
          "startLine": 401,
          "highlightLines": [
            404,
            411
          ],
          "lineNumbers": true,
          "layout": {
            "col": 1,
            "row": 4,
            "colSpan": 12,
            "rowSpan": 5
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "code-swap",
          "explanation": "One atomic swap moves ownership of the task reference in or out of the cell, so the owner and a stealer can never both get the same task. PhantomData<S> remembers the scheduler type erased by the raw pointer.",
          "sourceRefs": [
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "path": "tokio/src/runtime/task/atomic_notified.rs",
              "startLine": 28,
              "endLine": 39,
              "revision": "head"
            }
          ],
          "tone": "neutral",
          "type": "code-block",
          "label": "task/atomic_notified.rs · AtomicNotified::swap",
          "language": "rust",
          "code": "pub(crate) fn swap(&self, task: Option<Notified<S>>) -> Option<Notified<S>> {\n    let new = task\n        .map(|t| t.into_raw().header_ptr().as_ptr())\n        .unwrap_or_else(ptr::null_mut);\n    let old = self.task.swap(new, SeqCst);\n    NonNull::new(old).map(|ptr| unsafe {\n        // Safety: since we only allow tasks with the same scheduler type to\n        // be placed in this cell, we know that the pointed task's scheduler\n        // type matches the type parameter S.\n        Notified::from_raw(RawTask::from_raw(ptr))\n    })\n}",
          "startLine": 28,
          "highlightLines": [
            32
          ],
          "lineNumbers": true,
          "layout": {
            "col": 1,
            "row": 4,
            "colSpan": 12,
            "rowSpan": 5
